{:edb/db-before-t 211 :edb/db-after-t 212 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533524 50 #inst "2026-10-11T05:36:01.299Z" 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186124495 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406912 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186124495 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406913 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186124496 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406911 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186124496 1038 #edb/ref 17592186406914 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186125251 1068 #edb/ref 17592186124076 13194139533524 17592186045585 false] [17592186125251 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406908 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186125251 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186125251 1071 "Consider the vector space $M_{2}(R)$ of all $2 \\cdot 2$ matrices over $R$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. ${\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a linearly independent set in $M_{2}(R)$\n2. $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}$\n3. ${\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a basis of $M_{2}(R)$" 13194139533524 17592186045585 false] [17592186125251 1071 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- ${[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186125251 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-matrix is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]=0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406915 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406916 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406917 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406918 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406919 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1045 "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces" 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1046 #edb/ref 17592186406915 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046679 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048558 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406880 1053 #uuid "7a9a1a68-93b3-5d77-a9f3-56fa1ac555d7" 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406881 1081 "I only" 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406881 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533524 17592186045585 true] [17592186406881 1084 #uuid "04483552